  "limitations": [
    "The scale adapter is trusted and source-bound to the frozen Case06 operation chain, but it does not execute the GLM-produced migrated.py artifact.",
    "Scale scopes are separate distributions; their medians must not be summed and described as end-to-end latency.",
    "The private native core is unsupported and diagnostic-only.",
    "Each timing distribution has seven samples, fixed CPU-then-NPU order, no confidence interval and no randomized interleaving.",
    "The scale adapter uses constant finite inputs and does not cover random, NaN, Inf or boundary-value distributions.",
    "The 1M and 9M NPU samples include visible high-tail variation, especially allocation, public compute and H2D.",
    "Cold means a fresh process only; device, driver, filesystem and other machine-global caches are not reset.",
    "The NPU scale process has nine OS threads while all threads share one host-core affinity and observed OpenBLAS uses one thread; describe this as one host-core affinity, not a one-thread process."
  ]
}
